@startuml part-block-layout
' ============================================================================
' part-block-layout.puml — how nodes are packed within a 256 KB block:
' header · node directory (offset/len entries) · node data · free space.
' Source: docs/theory/disk-tries/04-persistent-art.md, § Block Layout.
' Drawn as a CONTIGUOUS colored region table (region + contents columns) hosted in
' a floating note; rows share borders (no gaps). Full-cell color via Creole |<#hex>|
' cells. The variable-length directory detail is split across adjacent same-color
' rows (Creole cells do not support in-cell line breaks).
' Color key:  amber #FFE0B2  block header (metadata)
'             blue  #BBDEFB  node directory (offset/len index)
'             green #C8E6C9  node data (the packed node payloads)
'             grey  #ECEFF1  free space
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam TitleFontSize 15
skinparam noteFontSize 14
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #37474F
}

title Node packing within a 256 KB block

note as BL
|= region |= contents |
|<#FFE0B2> Header  (64 B) |<#FFE0B2> block metadata |
|<#BBDEFB> Node Directory |<#BBDEFB> entry[0]  off 64 · len 48 |
|<#BBDEFB> offset/len index |<#BBDEFB> entry[1]  off 112 · len 160 |
|<#BBDEFB> (variable) |<#BBDEFB> entry[2]  off 272 · len 656  · … |
|<#C8E6C9> Node Data |<#C8E6C9> [Node4 @64] [Node16 @112] [Node48 @272] [Node4 @928] … |
|<#ECEFF1> Free Space |<#ECEFF1> unused tail |
end note

legend bottom
| Color | Region |
|<#FFE0B2>| block header (metadata) |
|<#BBDEFB>| node directory (offset/len index) |
|<#C8E6C9>| packed node data |
|<#ECEFF1>| free space |
endlegend
@enduml
